        <mxCell id="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-178" value="ITEM to VENDOR_ITEM" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=none;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=16;" vertex="1" parent="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-177">
          <mxGeometry width="160" height="450" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="160" height="450" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-179" value="one mandatory to many mandatory&lt;br&gt;(1,1) to (1,N)&lt;br&gt;1:1..*" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=none;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=16;" vertex="1" parent="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-177">
          <mxGeometry x="160" width="160" height="450" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="160" height="450" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-180" value="From VENDOR_ITEM: An item purchased from a vendor creates a VENDOR_ITEM entity, this is attached to a minimum and maximum of one ITEM entity because it represents that stock in the store. QuantityOnHand will increase in the exact difference when QuantityOnOrder decreases when OrderDueDate is reached compared to the current date. To increase accuracy, a boolean value of OrderReceived can also be added, if orders aren&#39;t timely." style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=none;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=16;" vertex="1" parent="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-177">
          <mxGeometry x="320" width="240" height="450" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="240" height="450" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-186" value="From ITEM: An ITEM entity always comes from a VENDOR_ITEM entity, so a minimum of one is mandatory. An ITEM entity can also be ordered from a different VENDOR which would be a different VENDOR_ITEM, which is why the maximum is many." style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=none;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=16;" vertex="1" parent="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-177">
          <mxGeometry x="560" width="240" height="450" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="240" height="450" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-181" value="" style="shape=tableRow;horizontal=0;startSize=0;swimlaneHead=0;swimlaneBody=0;strokeColor=inherit;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;collapsible=0;dropTarget=0;fillColor=none;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;fontSize=16;" vertex="1" parent="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-172">
          <mxGeometry y="590" width="800" height="380" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-182" value="VENDOR to VENDOR_ITEM" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=none;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=16;" vertex="1" parent="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-181">
          <mxGeometry width="160" height="380" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="160" height="380" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-183" value="one mandatory to many optional&lt;br&gt;(1,1) to (0,N)&lt;br&gt;1:M" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=none;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=16;" vertex="1" parent="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-181">
          <mxGeometry x="160" width="160" height="380" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="160" height="380" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-184" value="From VENDOR_ITEM: A VENDOR_ITEM entity has a minimum of one VENDOR entity and a maximum of one VENDOR entity. This is because the VENDOR_ITEM is purchased from that specific vendor and only that VENDOR entity shares the relationship with that VENDOR_ITEM. If it is a different VENDOR, it will generate it&#39;s own unique VENDOR_ITEM. This is also why VENDOR_ITEM is an associate entity, it is the link between the two strong entities VENDOR and ITEM." style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=none;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=16;" vertex="1" parent="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-181">
          <mxGeometry x="320" width="240" height="380" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="240" height="380" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-187" value="From VENDOR: A VENDOR entity can be entered into the database without ever making a purchase yet, hence a minimum of zero. A VENDOR entity can then also sell multiple different items to the shop, generated many VENDOR_ITEM entities, which leads to why the maximum is many." style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=none;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=16;" vertex="1" parent="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-181">
          <mxGeometry x="560" width="240" height="380" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="240" height="380" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="6g9lBCm_78rU3AsJnXWU-167" value="VENDOR_ITEM" style="shape=table;startSize=30;container=1;collapsible=1;childLayout=tableLayout;fixedRows=1;rowLines=0;fontStyle=1;align=center;resizeLast=1;html=1;fontSize=12;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="270" y="530" width="180" height="120" as="geometry" />
